  characterName: Paula Santos
  promptText: Funding from oil companies could keep my climate lab afloat but requires
    gagging critical findings about fossil fuels. Accepting preserves jobs and research
    capacity under constraints; refusing upholds integrity but may close the lab
    and displace staff.
  leftAnswer: Taking the funds keeps your team working and the lab running for now.
  rightAnswer: Refusing protects scientific integrity and public trust despite the
    cost.
